Found while doing this: the interface driver aimed every click tens of pixels
wide, because it took the window's position inside its frame for its position
on screen. That is why an earlier session concluded synthetic input does not
arrive here and wrote that into the tool documentation as fact. Both the code
and the documentation are corrected, and the corrected driver was used to open
the menu and submenu from coordinates read off a captured image.
